      "node_id": "kg_doc_6",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Title: A Kiss for Corliss. A Kiss for Corliss is a 1949 American comedy film directed by Richard Wallace and written by Howard Dimsdale. It stars Shirley Temple in her final starring role as well as her final film appearance. It is a sequel to the 1945 film \"Kiss and Tell\". \"A Kiss for Corliss\" was retitled \"Almost a Bride\" before release and this title appears in the title sequence. The film was released on November 25, 1949, by United Artists.",
